SECTOR FUNCTION – MASTER ARCHITECTURE
======================================

GOAL
-----
Provide a macro-to-micro analytical layer that:
- Classifies raw material sectors
- Determines cycle phase
- Feeds interpretation into producer ranking
- Does NOT modify internal corporate math (NPV, FCFF, etc.)
- Remains read-only and non-circular

------------------------------------------------------------
I. SECTOR DEFINITION LAYER
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Define the raw material universe and hierarchical grouping.

Structure:

Raw Materials (Top Level)
  ├── Precious Metals
  │     ├── Gold
  │     ├── Silver
  │     ├── PGM (Platinum, Palladium)
  │
  ├── Base Metals
  │     ├── Copper
  │     ├── Zinc
  │     ├── Nickel
  │     ├── Aluminium
  │
  ├── Energy
  │     ├── Oil
  │     ├── Gas
  │     ├── Uranium
  │
  ├── Battery / Strategic
  │     ├── Lithium
  │     ├── Graphite
  │     ├── Rare Earths
  │
  └── Bulk / Steel
        ├── Iron Ore
        ├── Metallurgical Coal

Each company:
- Can map to 1–N raw materials
- Has a dominant revenue driver (primary sector)
- Sector mapping stored in DB (company_sector_map)

------------------------------------------------------------
II. SECTOR DATA LAYER
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Collect and normalize sector-level data.

Inputs:

A. Price Data
   - Spot price
   - 1Y, 3Y, 10Y history
   - Percentile vs 10Y band

B. Supply/Demand Proxies
   - Production growth
   - Inventory levels (if available)
   - Capex trends (sector aggregated)
   - Exploration spending proxy

C. Equity Behaviour
   - Sector ETF performance
   - Relative performance vs broad market
   - Sector FCF trend (aggregate)

D. Macro Linkage
   - Real rates
   - Dollar index
   - PMI / industrial indicators
   - Inflation regime

All stored as:
- Raw time series
- Snapshot indicators
- Derived percentile scores (-2 to +2)

------------------------------------------------------------
III. SECTOR CYCLE ENGINE
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Classify sector phase without modifying corporate calculations.

Inputs:
- Price percentile (10Y)
- Momentum (12M change)
- Supply tightness proxy
- Capex expansion proxy
- Equity inflow behaviour

Outputs:

Sector Phase:
  - Early Cycle
  - Mid Cycle
  - Late Cycle
  - Compression
  - Structural Bull
  - Structural Bear

Also outputs:
  - Confidence score
  - Dominant drivers

Important:
- Sector cycle feeds into CYCLE ranking of companies
- It does NOT change their Structure score
- It does NOT alter discount rates

------------------------------------------------------------
IV. SECTOR DASHBOARD VIEW
------------------------------------------------------------

Displays:

1. Sector Overview
   - Phase
   - Price percentile
   - 1Y momentum
   - Macro sensitivity

2. Company Distribution
   - List of companies within sector
   - Structure score
   - Cycle score
   - Valuation anchor

3. Capital Allocation Heatmap
   - Sector-wide M&A intensity
   - Goodwill growth
   - Capex intensity

------------------------------------------------------------
V. SECTOR → COMPANY INTERACTION RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

Allowed:
- Sector phase influences company CYCLE score context
- Sector percentile used for interpretation banner
- Sector macro used for screening filters

Not Allowed:
- Sector phase altering NPV math
- Sector phase altering FCFF math
- Sector phase altering corporate Structure score

------------------------------------------------------------
VI. EDGE FUNCTION (Optional Advanced)
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Detect asymmetry at sector level.

Logic:
- High structural quality companies
- In sectors classified as Compression
- With attractive valuation anchor

Output:
Cross-sector asymmetry list

------------------------------------------------------------
VII. DESIGN PRINCIPLES
------------------------------------------------------------

- No circularity
- Sector does not write into corporate math
- Corporate Structure remains raw enterprise metric
- Sector layer is interpretive and comparative
- Developers handled separately
- Fully API-driven, no manual aggregation





SECTOR FLOW – END-TO-END (Macro → Sector → Company → Lists)
===========================================================

0) INPUT SOURCES (READ-ONLY)
----------------------------
A) Macro Layer (Layer 0)
   - macro_series_raw[t] (rates, DXY, PMI, inflation, etc.)
   - macro_snapshots (latest, deltas, 10y percentiles, score -2..+2)

B) Sector Data
   - commodity_price_series[t] per commodity
   - optional: inventories / supply proxies / capex proxies
   - equity proxies (sector ETF, relative strength)

C) Company Corporate Data (Producers only)
   - financial statements (IS/BS/CF) time series
   - market data (price, shares_current, market cap, debt, cash)
   - optional: SR-NAV anchor if available (project model output)

D) Mapping Tables
   - company_sector_map: company_id → {commodities[]} + primary_commodity
   - sector_hierarchy: commodity → category (precious/base/energy/etc.)


1) PIPELINE STEP: INGEST → NORMALIZE
------------------------------------
1.1 Macro ingestion:
   - store raw macro series
   - compute macro indicators (percentiles, z-like transforms)
   - write macro_snapshots (timestamped)

1.2 Sector ingestion:
   - store commodity price histories
   - compute sector price percentile (10y) + momentum (12m)
   - store sector_snapshots_raw (price, momentum, etc.)

1.3 Company ingestion:
   - store corporate statements + market fields
   - compute enterprise metrics (EV, debt, cash, OCF, FCF, EBIT, etc.)


2) ENGINE STEP: DERIVE SCORES (NO CIRCULARITY)
----------------------------------------------
2.1 Sector Cycle Engine (commodity-level)
   INPUT:
     - price_percentile_10y
     - price_momentum_12m
     - optional supply proxies
     - macro_snapshots (as context inputs)
     - equity behaviour proxies
   OUTPUT:
     - sector_phase ∈ {Compression, Early, Mid, Late, StructuralBull, StructuralBear}
     - sector_cycle_score (0..100 or -2..+2 internal)
     - confidence (0..1)
     - drivers[] (top contributing signals)
   WRITE:
     - sector_cycle_snapshot(commodity, ts)

   RULE:
     - sector engine may READ macro, may not write into macro
     - sector engine may not touch corporate math (NPV/FCFF)


2.2 Company STRUCTURE Engine (producer universe only)
   INPUT:
     - corporate historical metrics (5y–10y)
   OUTPUT:
     - structure_level_percentile (0..100) vs producer universe
     - structure_momentum_percentile (0..100) (3y trend vs universe)
   WRITE:
     - company_structure_snapshot(company_id, ts)

   RULE:
     - structure is commodity-agnostic (no sector inputs)
     - structure does not use price percentiles (avoid cycle bleed)


2.3 Company CYCLE Engine (producer universe only)
   INPUT:
     - company corporate LTM deltas (FCF acceleration, margin expansion, debt change)
     - sector_cycle_snapshot(primary_commodity) for context
     - macro_snapshots for context (optional)
   OUTPUT:
     - company_cycle_percentile (0..100) vs producer universe
     - cycle_flags (e.g., “cycle-boosted”, “cycle-compressed”)
   WRITE:
     - company_cycle_snapshot(company_id, ts)

   RULE:
     - cycle can READ sector+macro, but must be separable:
       (company cycle signal) + (sector context label)
     - cycle does NOT change structure scores


2.4 Company ASYMMETRY View (computed at query-time or snapshot)
   INPUT:
     - structure_level_rank
     - company_cycle_rank
     - valuation_anchors (EV/SR-NAV if available, EV/normalized_FCF)
   OUTPUT (display fields):
     - rank_delta = structure_rank − cycle_rank
     - sortable columns:
        structure_level, structure_momentum, cycle, rank_delta,
        EV/SR-NAV, EV/NormFCF, net_debt/EBITDA
   RULE:
     - no extra scoring; show columns + sorting


3) PRESENTATION LAYER (THREE PARALLEL LISTS + SECTOR DASHBOARD)
---------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 STRUCTURE LIST (global, producers)
   - columns: company, structure_level, structure_momentum, key sanity metrics
   - default sort: structure_level desc
   - filter: commodity, category, geography (optional)

3.2 CYCLE LIST (global, producers)
   - columns: company, company_cycle, primary_commodity, sector_phase, confidence
   - default sort: company_cycle desc
   - banners: “Sector: Compression/Early/Mid/Late…”

3.3 ASYMMETRY LIST (global, producers)
   - columns: company, structure_level, cycle, rank_delta, valuation anchors
   - default sort: rank_delta desc (or EV/SR-NAV asc)
   - this is the “edge finder” without hidden weighting

3.4 SECTOR DASHBOARD
   - per commodity: phase, price percentile, momentum, drivers, confidence
   - distribution: companies mapped to sector (primary + secondary)
   - overlays: macro context cards


4) INTERACTION RULES (GUARDS)
-----------------------------
- Sector/Macro may influence ONLY:
    * cycle context labels
    * company_cycle score inputs (as context)
    * screening flags/banners
- Sector/Macro may NOT influence:
    * company_structure_level / structure_momentum
    * internal NPV/FCFF math (project/corporate)
- Pre-revenue developers:
    * excluded from producer universe
    * handled by separate developer/project mode (NPV/risk/dilution)


5) USER ACTION LOOP (HOW YOU USE IT)
------------------------------------
- Start at SECTOR DASHBOARD to see phase + confidence
- Jump to CYCLE LIST for macro/cycle positioning
- Jump to STRUCTURE LIST for long-term quality filter
- Use ASYMMETRY LIST to find:
    “high structure + low cycle + attractive anchor”
- Then open Single Stock page for deep dive (no automatic decision)






CYCLE ENGINE, PRODUCER UNIVERSE (Corporate-level, sector-context, no segmentdata)
===============================================================================

MÅL
----
Ge en råvaruagnostisk, kvantifierad “Cycle score” per bolag (0–100 percentil),
som fångar nuvarande cykelmedvind, eller motvind, utan att blanda in STRUCTURE.

CYCLE ska kunna driva:
- CYCLE-listan (ranking)
- Kontext, banner, flaggor (”sector compression”, ”sector expansion”)
- Asymmetry-listan (via rank-delta mot Structure)

CYCLE får INTE:
- Ändra NPV, NAV, FCFF, discount rate, CAPEX-serier
- Ändra STRUCTURE-scoren
- Bli cirkulär mot valuation, dvs inte använda EV, multiplar eller pris på aktien

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
A) INPUTS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

A1. Company corporate signals (från standard statements)
- FCF_LTM, OCF_LTM, EBIT_LTM, EBITDA_LTM (om finns), annars EBIT proxy
- Revenue_LTM
- NetDebt_t0 (debt − cash), NetDebt_t0_minus_1y (om möjligt)
- Shares_current (för dilution trend om du vill, men helst STRUCTURE)

A2. Company baselines (historik, 5Y rullande)
- Median_5Y(FCF), Median_5Y(EBIT margin), Median_5Y(OCF), Median_5Y(Revenue growth)
- IQR_5Y (interquartile range) för robust normalisering, eller MAD

A3. Sector context (primary commodity)
- Sector phase label: Compression, Early, Mid, Late, StructuralBull, StructuralBear
- Sector confidence (0..1)
- Sector price percentile (10Y), och momentum (12M)
OBS: Sector input används som KONTEKST, inte som substitut för corporate-signal.

A4. Macro context (valfritt, men endast som kontext)
- Macro regime label och confidence
- Exempel: liquidity tight, real rates up, etc.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
B) NORMALISERING, hur vi gör det råvaruagnostiskt
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Grundprincip:
Jämför bolagets LTM mot bolagets egen historik, inte mot andra råvaror direkt.

B1. Robust z-lik transform per bolag
För varje signal X:
- baseline = Median_5Y(X)
- scale = IQR_5Y(X) eller MAD_5Y(X)
- z = (X_LTM − baseline) / max(scale, epsilon)
- clamp z till ett rimligt intervall, tex [-3, +3]

B2. Convert z till en 0..100 intern score per signal
- s = 50 + 16.67 * z    (så z=+3 ≈ 100, z=-3 ≈ 0)
- clamp s till [0, 100]

Poängen:
En uranproducent och en oljemajor kan jämföras på ”hur mycket bättre än sin egen norm”
de är just nu.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
C) CORE SIGNALS (minimalt, corporate-only)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Vi vill fånga tre saker:
1) Marginalexpansion och kassaflödesacceleration
2) Balansräkningsförbättring, eller stress
3) Toppen, eller botten, riskindikatorer via intern överhettning, utan prisdata

C1. FCF acceleration signal
- X = FCF_LTM
- baseline = Median_5Y(FCF)
- z_FCF = robust_z(FCF_LTM vs baseline)

C2. OCF quality signal (robusthet)
- X = OCF_LTM
- z_OCF = robust_z(OCF_LTM vs 5Y baseline)
OBS: om OCF inte finns, använd CFO proxy, men helst riktig OCF.

C3. Margin expansion signal
- EBIT_margin_LTM = EBIT_LTM / Revenue_LTM
- z_margin = robust_z(EBIT_margin_LTM vs 5Y baseline)

C4. Deleveraging signal
- NetDebt_change = NetDebt_t0 − NetDebt_t0_minus_1y
- Vi vill att skuld minskar, så vi inverterar tecken:
  z_debt = robust_z(−NetDebt_change vs 5Y baseline av förändringen)

C5. Revenue acceleration signal
- Revenue_growth_LTM = (Revenue_LTM / Revenue_LTM_minus_1y) − 1
- z_rev = robust_z(Revenue_growth_LTM vs 5Y baseline)

Minimikrav:
Du kan börja med C1, C3, C4.
C2 och C5 förbättrar stabilitet.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
D) SECTOR CONTEXT, som kontext, inte dubbelräkning
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

D1. Sector phase modifier (kontext, inte core)
Vi skapar en ”context label” och en mild justering, som aldrig dominerar corporate signal.

Exempel:
- Compression: context_bias = +5
- Early: +3
- Mid: 0
- Late: -3
- StructuralBear: -5
- StructuralBull: +2

D2. Confidence scaling
context_bias_effective = context_bias * sector_confidence

D3. Guardrail:
|context_bias_effective| max 7
Det ska aldrig ersätta corporate performance.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
E) AGGREGERING, inga interna viktmonster
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

E1. Company cycle raw score, 0..100
CycleRaw = mean( s_FCF, s_margin, s_debt, optional s_OCF, optional s_rev )
CycleRawAdj = clamp(CycleRaw + context_bias_effective, 0, 100)

E2. Convert till percentil i producer-universumet
CyclePercentile = percentile_rank(CycleRawAdj across all included producers)

Det är detta som rankar i CYCLE-listan.

E3. Flagging (för UX, inte score)
- If CycleRawAdj > 80 and sector_phase in {Late} then flag: “Late-cycle risk”
- If CycleRawAdj < 30 and sector_phase in {Compression} then flag: “Compression candidate”
- If z_FCF very high but z_debt very negative then flag: “FCF up, balance sheet stress”

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
F) MULTI COMMODITY COMPANIES
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

F1. Primary commodity rule
- All CYCLE context tas från bolagets primary commodity.
- Secondary commodities visas som metadata, inte i scoring.

F2. Optional advanced, om du senare vill
- Låt bolag ha 2–3 commodity weights, men detta kräver segmentdata, så default är OFF.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
G) DATA GAPS, graceful degradation
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

G1. Missing one signal
- Om en signal saknas, exkludera den från mean, minska confidence.

G2. Too short history
- Om < 3 års historik, använd 3Y baseline, sänk confidence.

G3. Negative revenue, eller nonsens
- Då kan margin bli instabil, fallback till EBITDA proxy om finns, annars exkludera margin.

G4. Universe inclusion
- Bolag utan meningsfull OCF historik exkluderas från producer-universumet, enligt din regel.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
H) OUTPUT CONTRACT (per bolag)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

CompanyCycleSnapshot:
- company_id
- ts
- cycle_raw_adj (0..100)
- cycle_percentile (0..100)
- sector_phase (label)
- sector_confidence (0..1)
- flags[] (strings)
- signal_components:
    z_FCF, z_margin, z_debt, z_OCF, z_rev (om beräknade)
    s_FCF, s_margin, s_debt, s_OCF, s_rev (om beräknade)
- confidence (0..1) baserat på datatäckning och historiklängd

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
I) PSEUDOCODE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

for company in producer_universe:
  signals = []

  z_fcf = robust_z(company.FCF_LTM, median5y(company.FCF), iqr5y(company.FCF))
  signals.append(to_score(z_fcf))

  z_margin = robust_z(company.EBIT_margin_LTM, median5y(company.EBIT_margin), iqr5y(company.EBIT_margin))
  if valid(z_margin): signals.append(to_score(z_margin))

  z_debt = robust_z(-company.NetDebt_change_1y, median5y(-NetDebt_change_1y), iqr5y(-NetDebt_change_1y))
  signals.append(to_score(z_debt))

  optional z_ocf, z_rev

  cycle_raw = mean(signals)

  context_bias = phase_bias(primary_sector.phase) * primary_sector.confidence
  cycle_raw_adj = clamp(cycle_raw + context_bias, 0, 100)

store cycle_raw_adj

after all companies:
  cycle_percentile = percentile_rank(cycle_raw_adj across universe)
  store snapshot with flags and components

